From c3c7ae12c317bf99c5bf10143c1eb3d76703312b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:19:09 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH 3/3] serial: sunsu: hand the console to firmware
 explicitly

Pin the console device and exclude removal, TTY reconfiguration and
native console writers before the caller captures other CPUs. Transfer
register ownership with a port trylock; no UART lock spans firmware.

Save configuration, mask interrupts and verify restoration before CPUs
resume. Preserve receive status and FIFO contents. Exceptional contexts
are refused, and console writers skip firmware-owned registers.

PC16550D SNLS378C sections 8.6.2-8.6.6 define DLAB, clear-on-read LSR,
write-only FCR and interrupt masking. The caller must contain a failed
restoration instead of resuming with uncertain UART state.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
